    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs could personalize explanations—adjusting step-by-step guidance for different skill levels. For example, they’d flag gaps (e.g., ‘You missed this rule’) or generate interactive problems tailored to student needs. My experience with creative problem-solving suggests LLMs could bridge gaps between abstract theory and practical application, making math feel less intimidating."
